-------------------------- MODULE MCRNResendTiming --------------------------
(***************************************************************************)
(* The instances of RNResendTiming.  MCRNResendTiming.cfg is the code's    *)
(* rule at the defaults with one tick of 500 ms: resend delay initial and  *)
(* maximum 2000 ms (4), the minimum rounded up to one tick (1),            *)
(* reliable_message_timeout 10 s (20), no back-off.                        *)
(* MCRNResendTimingBrokenBackoff.cfg is the first version's schedule with  *)
(* one tick of 100 ms: resend delay initial 1000 ms (10), maximum 2000 ms  *)
(* (20) and back-off to 8.  It must fail AttemptsBeforeTimeout: a sample   *)
(* sets rto to 1.5 s at the first tick, and the sends at 0, 1.5 and 4.5 s  *)
(* are all that fit before the timeout at 10 s, three where four are       *)
(* owed.  It passes ConfigAccepted, so the validation rule alone does not  *)
(* keep the property; it needs the delay without back-off.                 *)
(* MCRNResendTimingSeeded.cfg is the seeded start at the current defaults  *)
(* (2 s initial and maximum delay, the transport's round trip reported at  *)
(* 200 ms giving a 300 ms delay) and MCRNResendTimingBrokenUnseeded.cfg    *)
(* its reversed witness, the transport's round trip ignored: it must fail  *)
(* SeededGapBounded.                                                       *)
(***************************************************************************)
EXTENDS RNResendTiming
=============================================================================
